# Error summary

Summarise a failed submission before asking the user to find and fix individual fields.

These are civica reference implementations for component authors. They do not replace native Home Assistant behaviour or demonstrate a connection to a live home.

## When to use it

Use the summary even when one field needs correction. Put it at the start of the form content, below any back link, and use the same messages beside the fields.

## When not to use it

Do not use it for successful saves, general service notices or physical-device alerts. Do not show an error summary and an unrelated success banner as competing outcomes.

## Home Assistant adaptation

After a failed Home Assistant settings save, focus the summary once and preserve every non-secret answer. Prefix the page title with “Error:” when the form owns its page. In an existing modal, keep the focus inside that modal and use its accessible title; do not replace the application title indiscriminately.

## Accessibility and behaviour

Link each message to the affected control. For a grouped date, choose the first incorrect input; for radios, choose the first option. These static reference examples disable automatic focus on load so browsing this documentation is not interrupted.

